{
  "_README": "Labeled tile catalog consumed by furnish_building.py (and meant to be edited by an LLM/human placing tiles). Coordinates are (col,row) atlas cells on the named sheet; w/h is the object footprint in tiles. 'category' is one of floor|wall|window|door|furniture|prop|tree; furniture/prop also carry a 'room' or context tag. 'verified': true means the coordinate is taken from a known-good working palette (renders correctly in the map); false means it was read off an annotated contact sheet (region_grid.py / preview_catalog.py / catalog_web.py) and should be eyeballed before relying on it. Four sheets are addressable: franuka (32x32), school (16x16), bath (16x16) \u2014 the appended interior sheets \u2014 and kenney (27x18), the base outdoor tileset already in every map at firstgid 1. Curation note (2026-06-27): franuka furniture is kept to ONE colour per type for now (diversify later); the bath/school/kenney selections follow the user's region picks. Verify/browse tiles visually with: uv run python tools/geo/catalog_web.py --serve",
  "_llm_guidance": {
    "options_per_category": 12,
    "max_per_prompt": 30,
    "note": "When asking an LLM to choose tiles, show at most ~12 options per decision (one floor menu, one wall menu, a short furniture menu) and ~30 total in a single prompt. Past that, selection quality drops: the model starts ignoring options, repeating choices, or picking by list position rather than fit. Always pre-filter to the task (by sheet/category/room) instead of pasting the whole catalog, and prefer verified:true tiles \u2014 unverified ones are candidates, not guarantees."
  },
